e Junagadh Buddhist cave group [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khapra_Kodiya_Caves]; The Junagadh cave groups, which include the Khapra Kodiya Caves, are in Junagadh district, Gujarat, India [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junagadh_Buddhist_Cave_Groups]; The Khapra Kodiya caves are rooms carved in rock, built as monks'' quarters [SUPPORTED: https://gujarattourism.com/saurashtra/junagadh/buddhist-caves.html]; The caves were carved in rock under (during the reign of) Ashoka [SUPPORTED: https://gujarattourism.com/saurashtra/junagadh/buddhist-caves.html]; The caves lie along the edge of the Sudarshan Lake [SUPPORTED: https://gujarattourism.com/saurashtra/junagadh/buddhist-caves.html]; The Sudarshan Lake is vanished (no longer exists) [SUPPORTED: https://gujarattourism.com/saurashtra/junagadh/buddhist-caves.html]; They are the oldest of the Junagadh group of caves [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khapra_Kodiya_Caves]; Now only the highest story of the Khapra Kodiya caves remains [SUPPORTED: https://gujarattourism.com/saurashtra/junagadh/buddhist-caves.html]"}]'::jsonb),
