ify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Palaestra at Delphi is part of a gymnasium at the sanctuary of Delphi, Greece (central claim: a palaestra, the wrestling court of the Delphi gymnasium) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; That gymnasium is the oldest existing gymnasium of the Greek world [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The palaestra has a central court [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The court is ringed by columns (a peristyle) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The columns around the court are Ionic [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The columns around the court are of blue limestone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; Among the rooms was an undressing room (apodyterion) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; Among the rooms were rooms for ball play (sphairisteria) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; There were two such rooms for ball play [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]"}]'::jsonb),
