r and beast fights, in ancient Serdica). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphitheatre_of_Serdica]; The ruins lie in the centre of Sofia. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphitheatre_of_Serdica]; The amphitheatre was built on top of an earlier theatre. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphitheatre_of_Serdica]; That earlier theatre had been ravaged by the Goths. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphitheatre_of_Serdica]; It was built for up to around 25,000 spectators. [SUPPORTED: https://www.roamintheempire.com/index.php/2021/05/05/serdica-part-i/]; The ruins yielded a rare bronze medallion of Antinous. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphitheatre_of_Serdica]"}]'::jsonb),
