 Buckinghamshire, England) - central claim [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; The hill fort covers 15 acres [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; The fort may have been a refuge in times of strife [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; The remains of a clay-lined oven were found within the fort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; Hearths (fire-sites) were found within the fort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; Bloomery slag was found at the fort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; Hearths within the fort appear to have been used to smelt iron [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]; The refuge/strife use was during the Iron Age (the fort was only sparsely or intermittently inhabited then) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholesbury_Camp]"}]'::jsonb),
