s a funerary chamber [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]; The funerary chamber is covered (roofed) with large granite slabs - as built; the heritage record notes the main capstone now lies displaced on the west side of the structure [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]; Excavations took place in 1965 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]; The 1965 excavations unearthed slate tablets [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]; The 1965 excavations unearthed necklaces [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]; The 1965 excavations unearthed crosiers [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]; The 1965 excavations unearthed copper objects [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Dolmen_of_Zambujeiro]"}]'::jsonb),
